One way to change the odds here is to polymorph the shopkeeper. It's
random what he turns into, of course, so you might end up fighting an
arch-lich instead of a human -- but you very well might end up
fighting a rothe, or a tiger, or something else manageable.

If you do kill the shopkeeper, whether he's still human or not, you'll
be branded as a murderer, and receive the appropriate penalty. (Loss
of intrinsic telepathy, and two points of luck, and probably angering
the guard if you're in Minetown.)


